# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two jobs, and the first one matters more than the size saving: NOTHING HOLDING
# A SECRET MAY ENTER A BUILD CONTEXT. An image layer is readable by anyone who
# can `docker save` or `docker run` it, and a secret copied in and deleted in a
# later layer is still there. `orchestrator/.env` holds a live
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY on any machine that has run the Python CLIs directly, and
# `.env.docker` holds WEBGEN_MASTER_KEY — the key every stored API key is
# encrypted under. Both are excluded by name, not by a broad glob, so the
# exclusion is legible rather than incidental.

# ---- secrets ----
.env
.env.*
orchestrator/.env
# NOTE: deliberately NOT `**/.env*`. `editor/.env.hosted` must stay IN the
# context: it is what makes `npm run dev:hosted` hosted mode
# (VITE_WEBGEN_HOSTED=1), it holds no secret, and it is committed on purpose.

# ---- installed trees ----
# Reinstalled inside the image for linux-x64. Copying a Windows or macOS tree in
# would ship the wrong native binaries for @node-rs/argon2, esbuild, rolldown
# and lightningcss — and would then be shadowed by an anonymous volume anyway.
node_modules
**/node_modules
orchestrator/.venv

# ---- the tester's data ----
# Bind-mounted at runtime (compose.yaml), never baked in. `generated/` is 382MB
# of prior runs on the machine this was written on; `server/data/` is accounts,
# argon2 hashes, live sessions and encrypted API keys.
generated
server/data
data

# ---- local caches / run state ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
orchestrator/.kitaru
orchestrator/runlog

# ---- build & test artifacts ----
**/dist
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
coverage

# ---- VCS and tooling ----
# `.git` is excluded to keep the context small. The consequence is deliberate
# and recorded: `server/src/code-version.ts` shells out to `git rev-parse HEAD`
# and falls back to the "unknown" sentinel without a repo, which makes every
# job RESUME refuse with 409. compose.yaml bind-mounts the repo (so `.git` is
# present at runtime and the sha resolves for real); an image run WITHOUT that
# mount degrades to "unknown" — fresh jobs still run, only resume is lost.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.superpowers

# ---- docker's own files ----
Dockerfile
compose.yaml
.dockerignore
